# --- Private. Never commit anything below this line. ---
#
# This repo is public. `pro/` is the premium OCR block: published once under Apache-2.0, it is
# free forever, so a single mistake here is not repairable.
#
# This file is no longer the only protection: `scripts/private-gate.mjs` runs as gate 0 in CI and
# at release, and refuses to publish anything tracked below this line. It reads this list from its
# own copy on purpose, so that editing THIS file does not disarm it. But it only ever runs after a
# commit exists -- so the lines below are still what keeps the mistake from being made.
#
# `git add -A` and `git commit -a` respect these rules. `git add -f` does NOT -- except where the
# folder is a nested git repo (`pro/`, `.scratch/`), which stages nothing at all. Do not force-add
# anything below, and do not delete a line to "just check something".

pro/
.scratch/
.scratch-inspect/
.claude/
docs/agents/
Claude.md
PRD.md
skills-lock.json
tools/

# Local research notes, not part of the repo
docs/research/reddit-research-access.md

# The content patterns gate 0 matches against. They ARE the strings being protected -- an employer
# name, a ticket prefix -- so committing them would publish exactly what they guard. CI reads them
# from the PRIVATE_CONTENT_PATTERNS secret instead.
.private-patterns
